le=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I always liked Persephone a lot, what with her duel nature as both a goddess of the spring and the queen of the underworld. She was probably the goddess I always found the most interesting, so if I had to pick one I had a crush on it would probably be her.</div> </div> </div> </div>And her kisses taste like pomegranate!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-15T20:23:46-07:00","id":1129611,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1129320-gods-and-goddesses-you-have-crushes-on?p=1129549#post1129549\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Aaaaand now I'm terrified of how few goddess are ever explicitly sapphic. There goes my odds!</div> </div> </div> </div>I will fight to my dying breath to insist that Artemis &quot;forswearing the touch of man&quot; and running off to &quot;keep the company of maidens and nymphs&quot; was originally understood to mean something the ancient Greeks didn't actually have words for.<br /> <br /> Edit: Erzulie Dantor also claims gay women as part of her purview. I don't know whether most vodou practicioners interpret her as sapphic herself, but it seems like a valid read to me.<br /> <br /> I've got to believe Aphrodite and Ishtar are pan given their domains.<br /> <br /> You know Het-Heru better than me. Is she broadly a sex goddess or more specifically in the fertility sense?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 08-15-2017, 11:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-15T21:18:24-07:00","id":1129651,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1129320-gods-and-goddesses-you-have-crushes-on?p=1129611#post1129611\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I will fight to my dying breath to insist that Artemis &amp;quot;forswearing the touch of man&amp;quot; and running off to &amp;quot;keep the company of maidens and nymphs&amp;quot; was originally understood to mean something the ancient Greeks didn't actually have words for.<br /> <br /> Edit: Erzulie Dantor also claims gay women as part of her purview. I don't know whether most vodou practicioners interpret her as sapphic herself, but it seems like a valid read to me.<br /> <br /> I've got to believe Aphrodite and Ishtar are pan given their domains.<br /> <br /> You know Het-Heru better than me. Is she broadly a sex goddess or more specifically in the fertility sense?</div> </div> </div> </div>Het-Heru is a goddess and women and a goddess of love; it stands to reason she could be a goddess of women's love, and it's certainly how she speaks to me. I'm not as sure of her role as an outright sex goddess, academically, though I'll confess I've only ever really seen Bast presented in that light.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-15T21:37:45-07:00","id":1129658,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1129320-gods-and-goddesses-you-have-crushes-on?p=1129611#post1129611\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I will fight to my dying breath to insist that Artemis &quot;forswearing the touch of man&quot; and running off to &quot;keep the company of maidens and nymphs&quot; was originally understood to mean something the ancient Greeks didn't actually have words for.</div> </div> </div> </div>There were a ton of virgin goddesses in Greek mythology - Artemis, Hestia, Astraea, and probably plenty more whom I am forgetting. And yeah, Artemis was especially close to other women. I always imagined that some of these goddesses weren't interested in laying with men and were more interested in women, but like you said the Greeks hadn't really put a name to it yet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-15T22:04:07-07:00","id":1129675,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1129320-gods-and-goddesses-you-have-crushes-on?p=1129658#post1129658\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There were a ton of virgin goddesses in Greek mythology - Artemis, Hestia, Astraea, and probably plenty more whom I am forgetting. And yeah, Artemis was especially close to other women. I always imagined that some of these goddesses weren't interested in laying with men and were more interested in women, but like you said the Greeks hadn't really put a name to it yet.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> At my own table, I specifically interpret it to be the case with Artemis because she has the &quot;preferring the company of women&quot; element you don't have with the other virgin goddesses. Athena has one version of the Pallas myth that could be read that way, but personally I prefer to read her as ace.<br /> <br /> Hestia I find it more of a hook if she forgoes sex and relationships by political choice rather than personal orientation, because as the firstborn Olympian, a husband or son of her own could be seen as a threat to Zeus he would take umbrage to.<br /> <br /> (also I have an idea about the only being she ever loved I'm itching to use...)<br /> <br /> <br /> In terms of other Greek Goddesses - as I mentioned before, Aphrodite just makes sense as pan, and as they lack any myths linking them to men I'm aware of, I decided Tyche and Nemesis are a monogamous couple.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-16T03:59:32-07:00","id":1129734,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1129320-gods-and-goddesses-you-have-crushes-on?p=1129675#post1129675\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> At my own table, I specifically interpret it to be the case with Artemis because she has the &quot;preferring the company of women&quot; element you don't have with the other virgin goddesses. Athena has one version of the Pallas myth that could be read that way, but personally I prefer to read her as ace.<br /> <br /> Hestia I find it more of a hook if she forgoes sex and relationships by political choice rather than personal orientation, because as the firstborn Olympian, a husband or son of her own could be seen as a threat to Zeus he would take umbrage to.<br /> <br /> (also I have an idea about the only being she ever loved I'm itching to use...)<br /> <br /> <br /> In terms of other Greek Goddesses - as I mentioned before, Aphrodite just makes sense as pan, and as they lack any myths linking them to men I'm aware of, I decided Tyche and Nemesis are a monogamous couple.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wasn't Artemis sort of involved with Orion? But Apollo tricked her into killing him before it went anywhere?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8375-vonpenguin","name":"vonpenguin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-16T07:35:38-07:00","id":1129779,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1129320-gods-and-goddesses-you-have-crushes-on?p=1129499#post1129499\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Isn't the Forgotten Realms version just the Egyptian version? I remember the whole Netjer being there in.... Rashemen, I think?</div> </div> </div> </div> No. <br /> <br /> Okay short history of the Mulhorandi Pantheon (named after the Nation of Mulhorand). <br /> <br /> An Ancient and powerful empire of wizards called the Imaskar had a terrible plague and to make up for the lost population they kidnapped countless People from ancient Egyptian and various mesopotamian nations like Ayssria, Babylon, Summeria to be slaves. <br /> <br /> These slaves interbreed with the Imaskari,, each other, to become the Mulan.<br /> <br /> The Imaskari set up powerful magical barriers so that the Gods of the Mulan could come and liberate their people and kick the Imaskari's ass.<br /> <br /> Eventually even AO gets sick of this, so he tell Ptah, who in D&amp;D is also a God of wildspace to go tell the Mulan Gods what is going on.<br /> <br /> Some some of them (Bast, Ra, Geb, Anhur, Set, Isis, Orisis, Nerpthyr, Hathor, Horus, Ishtar, Inanna, Enlil, Gilgeam (Gilgamesh), Ninna Sin, Utu, and few other Gods, decide to get around the barrier with a nobel sacrifice, they assume mortal but ageless forms called Manifestations and have Ptah guide them to Toril. <br /> <br /> Once their they land their ships and create priests, divine minions, and incarnation (basically turning people into a mortal reincarnating avatar of themselves).<br /> <br /> Then crush Imaskar, freeing their people, but obliterating it in the process turning it into a desert. <br /> <br /> So they moved West into what ends up being Mulhorand for the former Egyptian Gods (Ra, Horus, Bast, Anhur, Isis, Osiris, Geb, Set, Sobek, Nethyr, Hathor). <br /> <br /> The rest move further west to found the nation of, Unther (Gods Enlil, Gilgeam, Ishtar, Inanna, Assuran (who becomes Hoar later) ect... <br /> <br /> Anyways some time after the Orcgate Wars during the peak of the second Mulhorand Empire, Bast absorbed Felidea a Beast Cult Goddess whose worship had appeared briefly in Mulhorand from nearby Barbarian tribes. <br /> <br /> This causes a personality shift in the War Goddess, who goes on walk about across the forgotten realms, when she visited the Yeirwood when it was being, attacked by the Drow. <br /> <br /> There a Goddess called Zandilar the Dancer, who was the last indiginious Yeirwood deity to not be absorbed by the Elven gods, was trapped by a Drow God she'd tried to seduce into helping her people, who in turn imprisoned her, hoping to consume her. Zandilar often seduced enemy Gods and Chieftians to protect her people. <br /> <br /> Bast distracted the Drow God, so Zandilar could escape, but Zandilar was so badly hurt and pregnate that she merged with Bast, also partly out of gratidude. <br /> <br /> Bast gave birth to a Drow God Sveltarm, but eventually Lloth (Sveltarm's grandma), tricks him into killing a demonlord, only to absorb its essence becoming corrupted and finding himself evil and Lloth consort. <br /> <br /> Because Bast absorbed Zandilar she's a Goddess of, Lust, not War now, and around the time of Myth Drannar (Elvish City) Bast ends up hooking up with Shar, Goddess of Night, to explore Plessures Darkside, where Bast gains her morr common name Sharess.<br /> <br /> Its a bad time for Sharess, and Shar tries to kill and absorb Sharess (Bast) during the time of troubles, but the Goddess of Beauty Sune saves Sharess by dousing her in the waters of Everbright. <br /> <br /> Since that time Sharess has been rebuilding her church which started to die off after she Hooked up with Shar.<br /> <br /> After ToTs Sharess moved to the Planes where the other Gods lived. <br /> <br /> Then the Spellplague happened, several of Sharess' temples were likely destroyed in the chaos, although her worship increased in Chessenta to help compensate for that. <br /> <br /> The Mulhorandi and Unther Pantheons are where gone except for those deities who ended up in the Faerunian Pantheon, such as Sharess (Bast), Hoar (Assuran), Tiamat, Baphmut (Marduk). <br /> <br /> This was exploited by survivors of Imaskar's, destruction from a city in the Underdark called Deep Imaskar. <br /> <br /> These Imaskari founded a new nation above ground called High Imaskar. <br /> <br /> Then the second Sundering happened and the Mulhorand Pantheon was reborn, and the Mulhorand crushed High Imaskar, driving its leadership into exile in the plains of purple dust, and to extra planar strongholds.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2241,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","user":"Omegaphallic","date":". 08-16-2017, 11:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-16T10:49:42-07:00","id":1129874,"title":"","content":"well, I must admit I have always kinda had a crush on Set for some reason. Hermes is also high on my list, and so does Apollo (even though I'll be scared to death to go on a date with him- it never seems to end up well in mythology!), and I've always had a weak spot for Triton. Baldr is kinda cute, but he lacks a bit of personality, and in general I have never found myself drawn to Norse deities (too macho for me, with the exception of Loki which may be a cool guy to go around with, but he's kinda stuck in the friendzone). Lugh is also hot, and I'm also kinda drawn to Arawn for some reason, even though he terrifies me. Inari and Tsukuyomi are also my type, and I'm kinda into the Babylonian Marduk and the Canaanite Shachar and Shalim. I also find Baron Samedi as a cool drinking partner- not sure about sex, but who knows what would happen after a few drinks, right? :P","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-16T11:10:24-07:00","id":1129886,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1129320-gods-and-goddesses-you-have-crushes-on?p=1129874#post1129874\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">well, I must admit I have always kinda had a crush on Set for some reason. Hermes is also high on my list, and so does Apollo (even though I'll be scared to death to go on a date with him- it never seems to end up well in mythology!), and I've always had a weak spot for Triton. Baldr is kinda cute, but he lacks a bit of personality, and in general I have never found myself drawn to Norse deities (too macho for me, with the exception of Loki which may be a cool guy to go around with, but he's kinda stuck in the friendzone). Lugh is also hot, and I'm also kinda drawn to Arawn for some reason, even though he terrifies me. Inari and Tsukuyomi are also my type, and I'm kinda into the Babylonian Marduk and the Canaanite Shachar and Shalim. I also find Baron Samedi as a cool drinking partner- not sure about sex, but who knows what would happen after a few drinks, right? :P</div> </div> </div> </div>Set/Sutek is a sneaky good choice. He's so loyal (Uesir excepted) and he's a cute redhead!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-16T11:17:05-07:00","id":1129891,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1129320-gods-and-goddesses-you-have-crushes-on?p=1129886#post1129886\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Set/Sutek is a sneaky good choice. He's so loyal (Uesir excepted) and he's a cute redhead!</div> </div> </div> </div>exactly! (10 more characters in order to post)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-16T13:36:47-07:00","id":1129956,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vonpenguin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1129320-gods-and-goddesses-you-have-crushes-on?p=1129734#post1129734\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Wasn't Artemis sort of involved with Orion? But Apollo tricked her into killing him before it went anywhere?</div> </div> </div> </div>That particularly story doesn't come from any source older than than the Roman writer Hygenius. Every original Greek version has him killed either by Gaia or Artemis for bragging he could slay every animal on the earth (a giant scorpion may or may not have been the weapon used to kill him, depending on the telling).<br /> <br /> Edit: actually his hubris/threat to animals is not the only motive for killing him in the Greek sources. Sometimes he actually assaulted Artemis or her retinue.<br /> <br /> So yeah, I definitely call bs on Hygenius' Roman version that caught on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 08-16-2017, 04:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-16T14:00:42-07:00","id":1129965,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1129320-gods-and-goddesses-you-have-crushes-on?p=1129956#post1129956\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So yeah, I definitely call bs on Hygenius' Roman version that caught on.</div> </div> </div> </div>well, considering that it is a Roman version, perhaps it wasn't Artemis that fell in love with Orion but Diana? I'm not sure how much their personality was different, but different mantles are different mantles.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-16T14:12:39-07:00","id":1129969,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1129320-gods-and-goddesses-you-have-crushes-on?p=1129965#post1129965\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">well, considering that it is a Roman version, perhaps it wasn't Artemis that fell in love with Orion but Diana? I'm not sure how much their personality was different, but different mantles are different mantles.</div> </div> </div> </div>Personally I'd rather use it as a story that Artemis hates in-setting and is worried about belief in it fatebinding her.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\"